  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<h2>Platform Types (Platform_Types)</h2><p class=\"lead\">Platform-specific fundamental data types (integers, booleans, floating-point numbers) mapped to CPU architecture primitives.</p>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<h3>Typen — Übersicht</h3>\n<ul class=\"mlist\">\n  <li><code class=\"sig\">typedef <a class=\"fn\" href=\"#SWS_Platform_00026\">boolean</a></code> <span class=\"dim\">This standard AUTOSAR type shall only be used together with the definitions TRUE and FALSE.</span></li>\n  <li><code class=\"sig\">typedef <a class=\"fn\" href=\"#SWS_Platform_00013\">uint8</a></code> <span class=\"dim\">This standard AUTOSAR type shall be of 8 bit unsigned.</span></li>\n  <li><code class=\"sig\">typedef <a class=\"fn\" href=\"#SWS_Platform_00014\">uint16</a></code> <span class=\"dim\">This standard AUTOSAR type shall be of 16 bit unsigned.</span></li>\n  <li><code class=\"sig\">typedef <a class=\"fn\" href=\"#SWS_Platform_00015\">uint32</a></code> <span class=\"dim\">This standard AUTOSAR type shall be 32 bit unsigned.</span></li>\n  <li><code class=\"sig\">typedef <a class=\"fn\" href=\"#SWS_Platform_00066\">uint64</a></code> <span class=\"dim\">This standard AUTOSAR type shall be 64 bit unsigned.</span></li>\n  <li><code class=\"sig\">typedef <a class=\"fn\" href=\"#SWS_Platform_00016\">sint8</a></code> <span class=\"dim\">This standard AUTOSAR type shall be of 8 bit signed.</span></li>\n  <li><code class=\"sig\">typedef <a class=\"fn\" href=\"#SWS_Platform_00017\">sint16</a></code> <span class=\"dim\">This standard AUTOSAR type shall be of 16 bit signed.</span></li>\n  <li><code class=\"sig\">typedef <a class=\"fn\" href=\"#SWS_Platform_00018\">sint32</a></code> <span class=\"dim\">This standard AUTOSAR type shall be 32 bit signed.</span></li>\n  <li><code class=\"sig\">typedef <a class=\"fn\" href=\"#SWS_Platform_00067\">sint64</a></code> <span class=\"dim\">This standard AUTOSAR type shall be 64 bit signed.</span></li>\n  <li><code class=\"sig\">typedef <a class=\"fn\" href=\"#SWS_Platform_00020\">uint8_least</a></code> <span class=\"dim\">This optimized AUTOSAR type shall be at least 8 bit unsigned.</span></li>\n  <li><code class=\"sig\">typedef <a class=\"fn\" href=\"#SWS_Platform_00021\">uint16_least</a></code> <span class=\"dim\">This optimized AUTOSAR type shall be at least 16 bit unsigned.</span></li>\n  <li><code class=\"sig\">typedef <a class=\"fn\" href=\"#SWS_Platform_00022\">uint32_least</a></code> <span class=\"dim\">This optimized AUTOSAR type shall be at least 32 bit unsigned.</span></li>\n  <li><code class=\"sig\">typedef <a class=\"fn\" href=\"#SWS_Platform_00023\">sint8_least</a></code> <span class=\"dim\">This optimized AUTOSAR type shall be at least 8 bit signed.</span></li>\n  <li><code class=\"sig\">typedef <a class=\"fn\" href=\"#SWS_Platform_00024\">sint16_least</a></code> <span class=\"dim\">This optimized AUTOSAR type shall be at least 16 bit signed.</span></li>\n  <li><code class=\"sig\">typedef <a class=\"fn\" href=\"#SWS_Platform_00025\">sint32_least</a></code> <span class=\"dim\">This optimized AUTOSAR type shall be at least 32 bit signed.</span></li>\n  <li><code class=\"sig\">typedef <a class=\"fn\" href=\"#SWS_Platform_00041\">float32</a></code> <span class=\"dim\">This standard AUTOSAR type shall follow the 32-bit binary interchange format according to IEEE 754-2008 with encoding...</span></li>\n  <li><code class=\"sig\">typedef <a class=\"fn\" href=\"#SWS_Platform_00042\">float64</a></code> <span class=\"dim\">This standard AUTOSAR type shall follow the 64-bit binary interchange format according to IEEE 754-2008 with encoding...</span></li>\n  <li><code class=\"sig\">typedef <a class=\"fn\" href=\"#SWS_Platform_91001\">VoidPtr</a></code> <span class=\"dim\">This standard AUTOSAR type shall be a void pointer Note: This type shall be used for buffers that contain data returned to the...</span></li>\n  <li><code class=\"sig\">typedef <a class=\"fn\" href=\"#SWS_Platform_91002\">ConstVoidPtr</a></code> <span class=\"dim\">This standard AUTOSAR type shall be a void pointer to const.</span></li>\n  <li><code class=\"sig\"><a class=\"fn\" href=\"#SWS_Platform_00064\">CPU_TYPE</a></code> <span class=\"dim\">This symbol shall be defined as #define having one of the values CPU_TYPE_8, CPU_TYPE_16, CPU_TYPE_32 or CPU_TYPE_64 according...</span></li>\n  <li><code class=\"sig\"><a class=\"fn\" href=\"#SWS_Platform_00038\">CPU_BIT_ORDER</a></code> <span class=\"dim\">This symbol shall be defined as #define having one of the values MSB_FIRST or LSB_FIRST according to the platform.</span></li>\n  <li><code class=\"sig\"><a class=\"fn\" href=\"#SWS_Platform_00039\">CPU_BYTE_ORDER</a></code> <span class=\"dim\">This symbol shall be defined as #define having one of the values HIGH_BYTE_FIRST or LOW_ BYTE_FIRST according to the platform.</span></li>\n  <li><code class=\"sig\"><a class=\"fn\" href=\"#SWS_Platform_00056\">TRUE_FALSE</a></code> <span class=\"dim\">The symbols TRUE and FALSE shall be defined as follows: #ifndef TRUE #define TRUE 1 #endif #ifndef FALSE #define FALSE 0 #endif</span></li>\n</ul>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
